Z||000000||TN Fieros||08-30-2001||12:18 AM||||Our next meet will be held Saturday, September the 8th. We will be meeting at Sonic in Lakewood, which is Northeast of Nashville. Meeting time is 12:30pm. After lunch we will cruise to a local park.<P>If you will be coming in in from either Memphis, get on I-65N when you get to Nashville and go to Exit 92. Get off of the exit and take a right. This is Madison/Old Hickory Blvd. You will stay straight on this road and go through several lights and then cross a big stone bridge. The Sonic is about 4-5 miles beyond the bridge on the right.<P>If you are coming from Knoxville, look for Exit 221 on I-40. Take a right off of the exit and go straight. This is Old Hickory Blvd. You will pass The Hermitage on your right. The Sonic is just beyond the little town of Lakewood and will be on your left.<P>From Chattanooga, you will get on I-40 or I-65 from I-24.. Either way is about the same distance. I personally think I-65 is easier.<P>We should have 10-12 cars there this month and hope to see you there!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TNFiero[1].gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000001||TN Fieros||09-02-2001||12:07 PM||||Next weekend! Just a reminder...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TNFiero[1].gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||14
Z||000002||Butter||09-04-2001||05:19 PM||||TN Fieros,<BR>Won't be able to make it this time.<BR>Hope yall don't think it's a crime.<BR>But one of the meets I'll will attend again.<BR>You'll know its me by my big gut and grin. <BR>Here's a wishin' yall all have fun.<BR>And I'll see yall again when I'm not under the gun.<P>Best Wishes for yall from<BR>Butter||||reg||12
Z||000003||ironhedno3||09-04-2001||09:30 PM||||hey folks as far as the cruise to the park im thinkin of taking old hickory blvd to briley pkwy west to harding road and the bunch of us going through belle mead and cruising percy warner park..and yes i will keep it at the speed limit so all can keep up..its kinda of a long run but the scenery is very nice..hope we dont get rained out..keith||||reg||6
